The ground, your formation, and your condition shape a battle.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Clusters and sweeping blows</ansi>

Shower of Sparks hits its chosen enemy's cell and the cells immediately
above, below, left, and right (orthogonal neighbors). It does not hit diagonals or chain through
neighbors. Targets must still be alive, visible, and in that battle when
the chant finishes. A fallen primary target stops the spell; it does not
move to another cluster. Spread out to reduce the damage to your company.

Some enemies, including forest ogres, sweep the whole front row. A sweep
takes one action, strikes each living front-row opponent once, and is
available again after three combat rounds. Shields, armor, and guardians
still protect against each strike. It never hits spectators or waiting bands.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Leaping and open flanks</ansi>

Some beasts, including timber wolves, leap past a missing, fallen, or
knocked-down front-line protector to strike the middle or back row. A
standing protector blocks the leap. A leap replaces a normal attack and
is available again after three combat rounds; guardians can still step in.

A rear member is exposed to melee when their own front column and an
adjacent front column are both open. Keep a standing front line: a
knocked-down member no longer closes a flank.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Narrow ground</ansi>

On narrow ground, such as the ruined Forest bridge, both lines fold into
two columns. Your saved formation is unchanged. Members keep their row
when possible, then spill backward, then forward into a vacancy. Any
overflow stands in reserve: it cannot make melee attacks or guard, but
can use ranged attacks or spells and can be targeted at range. Reserves
fill vacancies as members fall. The browser Battle view shows the current
positions; formation shows your saved arrangement.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Fatigue and numb hands</ansi>

Remaining Fatigue 51-100 has no hit penalty. Tired (26-50) lowers physical
hit chance by 5 percentage points; Exhausted (1-25) by 10; Collapsed (0)
by 20. The usual minimum hit chance still applies. Strikes name the penalty.
Rest before fighting; combat itself adds no new fatigue drain.

Frostbitten, Hypothermic, or Freezing to Death adds one combat round to
each new spell chant or sling shot. Chilled alone adds no extra round.
The cold's existing stat penalties still apply. Warming up helps your next
action; it never resets a chant already underway. Bows are not delayed.

See help ambush, help formation, help survival, help temperature, and help combat.
